---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const structuredData = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "Sydney vs Melbourne vs Brisbane — Best City for Kiwis Moving to Australia (2026)",
  "description": "Compare Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane for Kiwis moving to Australia. Costs, jobs, lifestyle, weather, and which city suits you best.",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "GoAustralia" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "GoAustralia", "url": "https://goaustralia.co.nz" },
  "datePublished": "2026-06-27",
  "dateModified": "2026-06-27",
  "mainEntityOfPage": "https://goaustralia.co.nz/sydney-vs-melbourne-vs-brisbane"
});
---
<Base
  title="Sydney vs Melbourne vs Brisbane — Best City for Kiwis (2026)"
  description="Which Australian city is best for Kiwis? Compare Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane — jobs, cost of living, weather, lifestyle, and Kiwi communities. Updated 2026 guide for New Zealanders."
  structuredData={structuredData}
>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides">Guides</a> / Sydney vs Melbourne vs Brisbane</div>
      <h1>Sydney vs Melbourne vs Brisbane — Which City Is Best for Kiwis?</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">Over 670,000 Kiwis live in Australia. Here's how the three most popular cities compare — costs, jobs, weather, lifestyle, and where you'll feel most at home.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell-narrow">

      <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:40px">
        <div style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:14px">Quick summary</div>
        <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px">
          <li><strong style="color:var(--amber)">Sydney</strong> — highest salaries but highest costs. Best for ambitious careers in finance, tech, and professional services. Harbour lifestyle, expensive housing.</li>
          <li><strong style="color:var(--amber)">Melbourne</strong> — best culture and food scene. Strong for creative industries, education, and healthcare. More affordable than Sydney, cooler weather.</li>
          <li><strong style="color:var(--amber)">Brisbane</strong> — fastest growing, most affordable of the three. Best weather year-round. Booming infrastructure with 2032 Olympics. Big Kiwi community in Logan and Gold Coast.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <article class="article">

        <h2>Cost of Living Comparison</h2>
        <p>All three cities are more expensive than most NZ cities, but Australian salaries are typically 15–30% higher. Here's how they stack up:</p>
        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Monthly Expense</th>
                <th>Sydney (AUD)</th>
                <th>Melbourne (AUD)</th>
                <th>Brisbane (AUD)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>2-bed apartment (inner city)</td><td>$3,200–$4,000</td><td>$2,400–$3,200</td><td>$2,200–$2,800</td></tr>
              <tr><td>2-bed apartment (suburbs)</td><td>$2,200–$2,800</td><td>$1,800–$2,400</td><td>$1,600–$2,200</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Groceries (family of 4)</td><td>$900–$1,100</td><td>$800–$1,000</td><td>$750–$950</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Public transport (monthly pass)</td><td>$200</td><td>$170</td><td>$155</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Childcare (per child/month)</td><td>$2,200–$2,800</td><td>$1,800–$2,400</td><td>$1,600–$2,200</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Electricity + gas</td><td>$250–$350</td><td>$220–$320</td><td>$200–$300</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)">Figures are approximate 2026 averages. Rent is the biggest variable — suburbs and location choice have a massive impact.</p>

        <h2>Jobs &amp; Salaries</h2>
        <p>As a New Zealand citizen, you can work in Australia immediately on your Special Category Visa (subclass 444). No application needed — just arrive.</p>
        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Industry / Role</th>
                <th>Sydney</th>
                <th>Melbourne</th>
                <th>Brisbane</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Software engineer</td><td class="price">$120–$170k</td><td class="price">$110–$155k</td><td class="price">$100–$145k</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Registered nurse</td><td class="price">$80–$100k</td><td class="price">$75–$95k</td><td class="price">$72–$90k</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Electrician / plumber</td><td class="price">$90–$130k</td><td class="price">$85–$120k</td><td class="price">$80–$115k</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Teacher</td><td class="price">$80–$110k</td><td class="price">$75–$105k</td><td class="price">$72–$100k</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Median salary (all roles)</td><td class="price">$85,000</td><td class="price">$80,000</td><td class="price">$78,000</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p><strong>Key industries by city:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sydney</strong> — finance, banking, tech, professional services, media</li>
          <li><strong>Melbourne</strong> — education, healthcare, creative industries, hospitality, retail HQs</li>
          <li><strong>Brisbane</strong> — mining services, construction (Olympics boom), government, tourism, logistics</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Weather &amp; Lifestyle</h2>
        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th></th>
                <th>Sydney</th>
                <th>Melbourne</th>
                <th>Brisbane</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Summer highs</td><td>26–30°C</td><td>25–30°C</td><td>30–33°C</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Winter lows</td><td>8–12°C</td><td>4–8°C</td><td>10–15°C</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Rain days/year</td><td>~100</td><td>~110</td><td>~85</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Sunshine hours/year</td><td>~2,500</td><td>~2,200</td><td>~2,900</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Beach access</td><td>World-class (Bondi, Manly)</td><td>Port Phillip Bay beaches</td><td>Gold Coast 1hr south</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Vibe</td><td>Fast-paced, cosmopolitan</td><td>Cultural, artsy, foodie</td><td>Relaxed, outdoorsy</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>Where Kiwis Live</h2>
        <p>There's a large New Zealand diaspora in all three cities. Here's where you'll find the biggest Kiwi communities:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sydney</strong> — Western Sydney (Parramatta, Blacktown, Liverpool), Northern Beaches. Large Pacific and Māori communities in South-West Sydney.</li>
          <li><strong>Melbourne</strong> — South-East suburbs (Dandenong, Springvale), Western suburbs (Werribee, Wyndham). Growing Kiwi community in inner-west.</li>
          <li><strong>Brisbane / Gold Coast</strong> — Logan (largest Kiwi community per capita), Ipswich, Southport, Coomera. Feels closest to NZ culture.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Shipping Costs by City</h2>
        <p>Shipping costs from NZ vary slightly by destination port:</p>
        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:20px 0">
          <table class="data-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Route</th>
                <th>Shared Container</th>
                <th>Full 20ft Container</th>
                <th>Transit Time</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Auckland &rarr; Sydney</td><td class="price">$2,500–$4,500</td><td class="price">$6,000–$9,000</td><td>3–4 weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Auckland &rarr; Melbourne</td><td class="price">$2,800–$5,000</td><td class="price">$6,500–$9,500</td><td>3–5 weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Auckland &rarr; Brisbane</td><td class="price">$2,500–$4,500</td><td class="price">$6,000–$8,500</td><td>3–4 weeks</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p><a href="/get-quotes">Get exact quotes for your route &rarr;</a></p>

        <h2>Our Verdict: Which City Should You Choose?</h2>
        <div class="checklist-box">
          <h3>Choose Sydney if...</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Your career is in finance, tech, or professional services</li>
            <li>You want the highest earning potential</li>
            <li>You value harbour views, beaches, and a buzzing city</li>
            <li>You're okay paying a premium for housing</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-box" style="margin-top:16px">
          <h3>Choose Melbourne if...</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>You love food, coffee, art, and culture</li>
            <li>You work in education, healthcare, or creative industries</li>
            <li>You want a more European-feeling city with distinct seasons</li>
            <li>You prefer better value housing than Sydney</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-box" style="margin-top:16px">
          <h3>Choose Brisbane if...</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>You want the most affordable big city</li>
            <li>You love warm weather year-round</li>
            <li>You want to be near a large Kiwi community</li>
            <li>You work in trades, construction, or logistics (Olympics boom)</li>
            <li>You want the Gold Coast lifestyle within reach</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="cta-box" style="margin-top:40px">
          <p>Ready to Move? Get Free Quotes</p>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--body);font-weight:400;margin-bottom:16px">Tell us which city you're heading to and get up to 3 quotes from verified trans-Tasman movers.</p>
          <a href="/get-quotes" class="btn btn-dark btn-lg">Get Free Quotes &rarr;</a>
        </div>

        <h2>Related Guides</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/shipping-to-australia-from-nz">Shipping to Australia from NZ</a> — how sea freight and air freight works, customs, timelines, and tips to save.</li>
          <li><a href="/moving-costs">Moving costs from NZ to Australia</a> — full breakdown of shipping, flights, accommodation, and setup expenses.</li>
          <li><a href="/moving-checklist">Complete moving checklist for Kiwis</a> — visas, TFN, Medicare, KiwiSaver, and everything to sort before and after you land.</li>
        </ul>

      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
